  "query_preview": "..\nNext 7 days (Through next Monday)...\n\nUpper level troughing and associated low pressure system will\ncontinue to move to the east today. High pressure being advected\nin behind the low will cool temperatures into the low to mid 80s F\nfor most. The Absaroka/Beartooth mountains have a 20-50% chance \nfor showers and thunderstorms while lower elevation will remain \ndry. \n\nUpper level ridging moves into the region Wednesday as upper level\nflow gets pinched between troughing to the east and west. This\npattern is expected to last through the middle of the week\nincreasing temperatures into the 90s F by Thursday. Starting \nFriday, ensemble systems are indicating that the 500 mb trough \nover the Pacific Northwest will begin to move to the east and \nflatten out the ridge. Increasing moisture Thursday through \nSaturday brings chances for showers and thunderstorms. Medium \nrange convective forecasts are indicating the potential for severe\nweather each of these days but there are no clear signals at this\ntime. This lowering of heights will lead to lower temperatures in\nthe 70s and 80s F by Sunday. Torgerson",
